ntinuously for up to 14 days; and Zio ECG Utilization Software System, which supports the capture and analysis of ECG data. In addition, the company offers Zio AT System, a prescription-only remote ECG monitoring system, which consists of the Zio AT patch that records the electric signal from the heart continuously for up to 14 days, as well as incorporates the Zio AT wireless gateway to provide connectivity between the patch and the ZEUS System during the patient wear period. It has a development collaboration agreement with BioIS to develop and commercialize pulse oximetry, accelerometry, and trending non-invasive blood pressure technologies for use within ambulatory cardiac monitoring products and services. The company was formerly known as iRhythm Technologies, Inc. and changed its name to iRhythm Holdings, Inc. in January 2026. iRhythm Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California."}}